Capture Anthropic's serving model when fallback happens after message_start.

Upstream records event.message.model as output.responseModel, but only from the
initial message_start. Fable can instead emit a fallback content block after
producing signed thinking, so the stream carries Fable- and Opus-signed blocks
while the finalized message stays labelled Fable. On the next turn Anthropic
rejects the Opus block when Pi replays it as Fable. Final usage iterations are a
second authoritative source when an intermediary omits the boundary block.

Keep responseModel and usage pricing aligned with the latest serving model. The
Fable extension then removes model-bound thinking from replay while preserving
the fallback's text and tool calls.

